luci-theme-design-x — third-party data attribution
===================================================

This package ships a generated runtime asset at

    /www/luci-static/design-x/data/oui.json.gz

which is the gzipped JSON form of the Wireshark `manuf` community-curated
MAC OUI database, restricted to 24-bit MA-L entries. The transformation is
performed in this project's CI pipeline (.github/workflows/build.yml) at
build time from the upstream URL

    https://www.wireshark.org/download/automated/data/manuf

The Wireshark `manuf` database is distributed under the GNU General Public
License version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later). See

    https://www.wireshark.org/about.html#licensing

The luci-theme-design-x theme code itself is licensed under the Apache
License 2.0 (see LICENSE in the project root).

License coexistence
-------------------

The GPL-2.0 data file and the Apache-2.0 theme code coexist within this
IPK as a "mere aggregation" per FSF guidance:

    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-faq.html#MereAggregation

The data file is consumed as a static lookup table by the theme's JS at
runtime. Neither the GPL data nor the Apache code is linked, statically
or dynamically, into the other's runtime image; they are independent
works distributed together for convenience.

Each component retains its own license; the combination in this package
does NOT relicense either side. Downstream redistribution must preserve
both this NOTICE and the upstream Wireshark licensing terms for the data
file.

Refreshing the data
-------------------

The data file is regenerated fresh on every CI build, so each released
IPK ships the latest OUI registrations available from Wireshark at build
time. We deliberately do NOT run a cron-style refresher on the router
itself; see doc/macvendor.md §七 #2 for the reasoning (flash wear,
silent network failures, freshness vs cost trade-off for a residential
router).

